   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The polite present: -아요 / -어요",
     "texto": [
      "In the dictionary, verbs end in **-다**: 가다 (to go), 먹다 (to eat). To speak, you remove 다 and add **-아요** or **-어요**. It is the polite form used every day.",
      "With regular verbs, if the last vowel of the stem is **ㅏ** or **ㅗ**, you add **-아요**: 가다 → 가요, 오다 → 와요, 보다 → 봐요.",
      "With any other vowel, **-어요**: 먹다 → 먹어요, 읽다 → 읽어요, 마시다 → 마셔요. There are some irregular changes, which you will learn with their examples.",
      "Verbs ending in **하다** become **해요**.",
      "The big advantage: the verb **does not change with the person**. 가요 is «I go», «you go», «he/she goes», «we go»… and it can also be used to ask questions."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
